## 8. Existing SHA-256 / hashing utilities

**File:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/HouseholdIdGenerator.java` — the only real SHA-256 hashing utility in `src/main`.

```java
public final class HouseholdIdGenerator {

    private static final int LENGTH = 12;

    private HouseholdIdGenerator() {
    }

    public static String generate(String lastName, String address) {
        String key = TextNormalizer.normalize(lastName) + "\n" + TextNormalizer.normalize(address);
        return shaHex(key).substring(0, LENGTH).toUpperCase();
    }

    private static String shaHex(String value) {
        try {
            byte[] digest = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256").digest(value.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
            StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder(digest.length * 2);
            for (byte b : digest) {
                sb.append(String.format("%02x", b));
            }
            return sb.toString();
        } catch (NoSuchAlgorithmException e) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("SHA-256 is required but unavailable", e);
        }
    }
}
```

Produces a 12-char UPPER-case hex prefix of SHA-256 over `normalize(lastName) + "\n" + normalize(address)`. Uses `TextNormalizer` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/TextNormalizer.java`). Called from `ClinicServiceImpl.joinHousehold` (lines 307-316).

The other grep hits for "hash" (`JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl` etc., and `Owner`/`Pet`/`User`/`Vet` models) are just `hashCode()`/`HashMap`/`HashSet` — not cryptographic. No `DigestUtils`/Guava hashing present.

